2. WhatsApp Web Tool

ISHA ko WhatsApp Web ke through message send karne ki capability chahiye.

Example user command:

WhatsApp Web kholo aur Rahul ko "Hello, kaise ho?" message bhejo.

ISHA ko samajhna chahiye:

Intent:
send_whatsapp_message

Recipient:
Rahul

Message:
Hello, kaise ho?

Then:

ISHA
 ↓
WhatsApp Web Tool
 ↓
Browser
 ↓
web.whatsapp.com
 ↓
User's existing WhatsApp Web session
 ↓
Search/contact selection
 ↓
Message
 ↓
Send

---

3. WhatsApp Login

WhatsApp credentials/password ko code me store mat karo.

WhatsApp Web ka normal login/session use karo.

First time:

Open WhatsApp Web
        ↓
User scans QR code
        ↓
WhatsApp Web session established
        ↓
Session/browser profile persist

Next time possible ho to existing authenticated browser profile/session reuse karo.

User ko har baar QR scan karne ki zarurat nahi honi chahiye, provided WhatsApp Web session remains valid.

---

4. Browser Profile

WhatsApp Web automation ke liye dedicated browser profile create karo.

Example concept:

isha_browser_profile/

Isme WhatsApp Web session persist ho sakta hai.

Important:

- WhatsApp login credentials manually save mat karo.
- Cookies/session data ko unnecessary expose mat karo.
- Existing browser automation architecture ho to usko reuse karo.

---

5. Recipient Validation

Message send karne se pehle recipient ko correctly identify karna important hai.

Example:

User:

Rahul ko message bhejo.

Agar multiple contacts matching "Rahul" milte hain:

Mujhe multiple Rahul contacts mile hain.
Kaunse Rahul ko message bhejna hai?

User confirmation ke bina wrong person ko message mat bhejo.

Possible matching information:

Name
Phone number
WhatsApp contact

jo WhatsApp Web interface safely expose karta hai.

---

6. Message Confirmation

Normal message sending ke liye user ko preview/confirmation dena preferable hai, especially jab recipient ambiguous ho.

Example:

Message ready:

To: Rahul
Message: Hello, kaise ho?

Send kar du?

User:

Haan

Then send.

Agar user explicitly command me clearly says:

Rahul ko abhi "Hello" bhej do

to existing permission policy ke according direct send possible hai, provided recipient unambiguous hai.

